WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:32.050 --> 01:33.760
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:33.843 --> 01:34.844
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:48.775 --> 01:50.485
Hey, look, Maomao.

01:51.861 --> 01:52.779
That’s amazing.

01:52.862 --> 01:54.572
Right?

01:54.656 --> 01:57.617
<i>I see, so you called me to show me this.</i>

01:57.700 --> 01:59.994
It’s an impressive mirror, isn’t it?

02:00.078 --> 02:02.122
Do you know what it’s made of?

02:03.373 --> 02:06.209
This reflection… is it made of glass?

02:07.293 --> 02:08.128
That’s correct.

02:08.711 --> 02:11.005
Wow, it’s like there are two of you,
Lady Gyokuyou.

02:11.840 --> 02:14.467
<i>Glass mirrors are difficult to make,</i>

02:14.551 --> 02:16.761
<i>and they can only be imported</i>
<i>from the West.</i>

02:16.845 --> 02:18.513
<i>They’re extremely high-end luxury items.</i>

02:19.389 --> 02:23.017
<i>If you accidentally break it, I wouldn't</i>
<i>even be surprised if you lose your head.</i>

02:23.101 --> 02:25.812
There was a glass hand mirror before too,

02:25.895 --> 02:27.438
but Yinghua broke it.

02:27.522 --> 02:30.024
Oh, stop bringing that up!

02:30.108 --> 02:32.610
<i>It’s a good thing that</i>
<i>Lady Gyokuyou is so forgiving.</i>

02:36.531 --> 02:38.366
Maomao, are you interested in this too?

02:38.449 --> 02:41.411
Yes. How is it constructed?

02:42.245 --> 02:43.746
If it could be mass-produced domestically,

02:43.830 --> 02:46.416
we could make a lot of money…

02:46.499 --> 02:47.750
Yeah, that’s true.

02:47.834 --> 02:49.794
This full-length mirror, you see,

02:49.878 --> 02:52.463
is a gift from an envoy
from a foreign country.

02:52.547 --> 02:53.923
An envoy, you say?

02:54.507 --> 02:57.510
<i>Now that you mention it,</i>
<i>that quack doctor did say something…</i>

02:57.594 --> 02:59.470
<i>The large caravan that arrived was</i>

02:59.554 --> 03:02.932
<i>supposedly the advance party</i>
<i>sent to welcome a foreign envoy.</i>

03:03.016 --> 03:06.519
It seems they’ve sent gifts
to other high-ranking consorts too.

03:06.603 --> 03:08.521
Don’t say it like that.

03:09.564 --> 03:12.400
<i>Including Consort Gyokuyou,</i>
<i>there are four high-ranking consorts.</i>

03:12.483 --> 03:15.695
<i>Even as an envoy, they can’t show</i>
<i>favoritism to just one person.</i>

03:16.738 --> 03:20.033
<i>Bringing four such</i>
<i>magnificent full-length mirrors,</i>

03:20.116 --> 03:23.703
<i>whether crossing the desert or the sea,</i>
<i>must have been quite the ordeal.</i>

03:24.704 --> 03:27.165
<i>To go to such lengths</i>
<i>to please the consorts,</i>

03:27.248 --> 03:31.210
<i>they might be proposing</i>
<i>some major trade deal with this country.</i>

03:32.462 --> 03:35.215
Xiaomao, do you have a moment?

03:35.298 --> 03:37.800
Lord Gaoshun, what brings you here?

03:38.676 --> 03:42.388
There’s something I’d like
your opinion on.

03:42.472 --> 03:44.557
Lady Hongniang, may I use
this space for a bit?

03:44.641 --> 03:46.976
Sure, I don’t mind,

03:47.060 --> 03:48.728
but is it something private?

03:53.107 --> 03:56.861
<i>Lady Hongniang also joined us saying that</i>
<i>it was not right for us to be alone,</i>

03:56.945 --> 03:58.988
<i>but after finding that</i>
<i>Lord Gaoshun has a wife and child,</i>

03:59.072 --> 04:01.157
<i>she apparently lost all interest.</i>

04:02.659 --> 04:05.495
I’m not sure how helpful I can be,

04:05.578 --> 04:06.621
but what is the talk?

04:07.538 --> 04:10.458
Actually, a friend of mine
is in a great deal of trouble,

04:11.334 --> 04:13.127
and it’s quite an unusual story.

04:14.545 --> 04:17.423
<i>There were two daughters</i>
<i>in a certain respectable family.</i>

04:17.507 --> 04:20.218
<i>The two sisters, who were close</i>
<i>in age and looked very similar,</i>

04:20.301 --> 04:22.720
<i>were raised with love by their parents,</i>

04:22.804 --> 04:25.932
<i>but by the time they were of age,</i>
<i>their parents became overprotective.</i>

04:26.891 --> 04:28.685
<i>Not only was one of them restricted,</i>

04:28.768 --> 04:31.396
<i>but neither of them</i>
<i>was allowed to go outside,</i>

04:31.479 --> 04:33.398
<i>and they were assigned</i>
<i>a maid to watch them.</i>

04:33.481 --> 04:35.942
<i>The sisters spent their days</i>
<i>confined to the house.</i>

04:37.151 --> 04:40.446
<i>The maid, feeling sorry for them,</i>
<i>occasionally took them out,</i>

04:41.072 --> 04:42.949
<i>but when their father found out,</i>

04:43.700 --> 04:45.952
<i>he placed a servant</i>
<i>outside their room to keep watch.</i>

04:47.287 --> 04:48.705
<i>At night, he locked the door,</i>

04:48.788 --> 04:51.040
<i>so they couldn’t leave.</i>

04:52.292 --> 04:54.252
<i>The originally introverted sisters</i>

04:54.335 --> 04:57.046
<i>spent their days</i>
<i>doing embroidery in their room,</i>

04:57.714 --> 04:58.840
<i>but one day…</i>

04:59.340 --> 05:00.883
Father, my sister…

05:01.676 --> 05:04.012
is carrying the child of an immortal.

05:07.515 --> 05:09.058
That’s…

05:09.142 --> 05:11.227
An odd story, indeed.

05:11.311 --> 05:14.022
Perhaps the maid secretly
took them out again?

05:14.105 --> 05:16.691
No, the maid who allowed them to go out

05:16.774 --> 05:18.901
was dismissed as a warning.

05:19.777 --> 05:22.822
The new maid didn’t have
much interaction with the sisters.

05:22.905 --> 05:26.451
Then… although it’s a shameless story,

05:26.534 --> 05:29.412
perhaps she had relations with the servant
who was keeping watch?

05:29.495 --> 05:31.956
That’s also difficult.

05:32.040 --> 05:34.208
The servant wasn’t even allowed to

05:34.292 --> 05:35.960
get close to the room for surveillance.

05:36.627 --> 05:38.880
It is indeed a difficult story, but…

05:38.963 --> 05:41.090
I don't think there is
anything I can help you with.

05:42.050 --> 05:45.219
If you'd like to know whether it's
possible for a woman to become pregnant

05:45.303 --> 05:47.930
without having relations with a man,
I can see where you're coming from.

05:48.014 --> 05:49.557
But is such a thing possible?

05:50.433 --> 05:52.643
It is not the actual conception
of a child,

05:52.727 --> 05:55.354
but rather the body's illusion
of pregnancy.

05:56.647 --> 05:58.191
<i>At a brothel, a young courtesan</i>

05:58.274 --> 06:00.318
<i>once told me that she was pregnant</i>

06:00.401 --> 06:02.361
<i>with the child of the man she loved.</i>

06:02.445 --> 06:05.198
She wasn’t actually pregnant?

06:05.281 --> 06:08.284
That’s correct.
Even so, her period stopped,

06:08.367 --> 06:10.328
and her chest and abdomen swelled.

06:10.411 --> 06:13.331
The effects of belief
on the body can be significant.

06:14.957 --> 06:17.585
Are you certain that
the younger sister became pregnant?

06:18.628 --> 06:20.046
Well… yes… probably…

06:20.129 --> 06:22.799
Let’s leave it at that.

06:24.133 --> 06:25.301
The issue is…

06:25.384 --> 06:28.846
whether the younger sister managed to
slip away unnoticed by the surveillance.

06:29.347 --> 06:33.309
So, do you know how the sisters
were being watched?

06:33.392 --> 06:36.020
Yes, I have a floor plan here.

06:38.648 --> 06:39.941
The sisters lived in

06:40.024 --> 06:42.777
a detached building on the north side,
which was connected

06:42.860 --> 06:45.321
to the main house by a western corridor.

06:45.404 --> 06:46.906
Where was the restroom?

06:46.989 --> 06:48.783
It was inside the detached building.

06:49.283 --> 06:51.619
If the younger sister were to escape…

06:52.120 --> 06:54.956
The only exit would be
the western corridor.

06:55.039 --> 06:57.959
There are windows
on the east and south sides,

06:58.042 --> 06:59.919
but the servants were keeping watch.

07:00.920 --> 07:03.548
Where were the servants stationed
to watch?

07:04.298 --> 07:06.801
<i>The south-facing windows</i>
<i>were being watched from the third floor,</i>

07:07.593 --> 07:10.805
<i>and the east-facing windows</i>
<i>were monitored from the first floor.</i>

07:12.473 --> 07:15.184
The visible range is quite limited,
isn't it?

07:15.268 --> 07:17.812
-The interior wouldn't be visible at all.
-Yes.

07:18.980 --> 07:21.315
<i>However, it seems the sisters</i>

07:21.399 --> 07:23.317
<i>often sat by the windows to do embroidery.</i>

07:23.401 --> 07:26.279
That’s quite an unusual hobby…
embroidery, of all things.

07:26.904 --> 07:29.031
It seems they were originally
a nomadic family.

07:30.074 --> 07:31.159
<i>I wonder…</i>

07:31.242 --> 07:35.037
<i>It feels like the key details</i>
<i>are being left vague somehow.</i>

07:36.038 --> 07:39.959
<i>The east and south windows</i>
<i>seem to belong to the same room.</i>

07:40.042 --> 07:43.045
<i>The bedrooms were arranged separately</i>
<i>for the sisters.</i>

07:43.671 --> 07:46.632
Was this detached building
originally meant for guests?

07:46.716 --> 07:48.426
You’re quite observant, aren’t you?

07:48.509 --> 07:51.471
-How many servants were watching it?
-Two.

07:51.554 --> 07:54.182
Each of them had the same
assigned position throughout.

07:55.850 --> 07:58.019
<i>He seems to know an awful lot of details.</i>

07:58.102 --> 08:00.605
<i>Yet, he's not sharing everything.</i>

08:00.688 --> 08:02.231
<i>This feeling…</i>

08:02.315 --> 08:05.359
<i>Is this really a story about a "friend"?</i>

08:06.068 --> 08:09.363
<i>Should I say something or just keep quiet?</i>

08:11.073 --> 08:12.492
I almost forgot, Xiaomao,

08:13.117 --> 08:15.161
I have something from Lord Jinshi.

08:15.244 --> 08:18.915
It is an apology for the delay
in the delivery of the ox bezoar.

08:19.707 --> 08:22.126
<i>Ox bezoar! Now that you mention it,</i>
<i>I haven’t received it yet.</i>

08:22.919 --> 08:26.631
<i>I kept quiet to avoid getting headbutted</i>
<i>again, but the delivery is late!</i>

08:27.215 --> 08:30.676
My apologies, but it seems the
demand has suddenly increased.

08:31.552 --> 08:33.095
Why all of a sudden?

08:35.640 --> 08:37.767
Recently, I’ve heard that…

08:37.850 --> 08:41.020
many people have been sending
rare elixirs to Lord Jinshi.

08:41.604 --> 08:44.565
It’s rumored that he’s been
eagerly searching for them.

08:44.649 --> 08:46.943
Well, that’s the gist of it.

08:47.026 --> 08:48.569
Anyway, here you go.

09:00.790 --> 09:02.333
What is that?

09:02.959 --> 09:05.711
-It's bear bile.
-It’s the dried gallbladder of a bear.

09:05.795 --> 09:09.924
Although it has a bitter taste, it is a
valuable herb used in digestive ailments!

09:10.007 --> 09:12.301
I’m glad you’re pleased with it.

09:12.385 --> 09:15.388
Originally, Lord Jinshi
wanted to hand it to you personally.

09:18.182 --> 09:21.644
So, did you notice anything
from what I mentioned?

09:22.645 --> 09:23.980
Understood.

09:24.063 --> 09:26.274
Could you please wait for a moment?

09:33.447 --> 09:35.575
Assuming these nuts represent the sisters,

09:36.158 --> 09:39.495
does this match where they usually sat?

09:39.579 --> 09:40.580
Yes, that’s correct.

09:41.163 --> 09:42.456
There were two servants watching.

09:42.540 --> 09:45.668
Each of them always kept watch
from the same position.

09:45.751 --> 09:46.586
So…

09:46.669 --> 09:50.089
What if we place a mirror like this?

09:51.674 --> 09:53.676
It's as if there's another nut.

09:54.468 --> 09:55.595
Similarly,

09:55.678 --> 09:59.640
what if there was a large mirror
near this eastern window?

10:00.391 --> 10:02.602
<i>From the watch position,</i>
<i>it would be too far away and</i>

10:02.685 --> 10:04.979
<i>hard to notice,</i>
<i>even if it seemed a little unnatural.</i>

10:05.563 --> 10:08.065
In other words,
only one person was actually in the room,

10:08.149 --> 10:11.152
and the other was simply
a reflection in the mirror?

10:13.070 --> 10:14.488
If the sisters look very similar,

10:14.572 --> 10:17.450
it might have been difficult
for the servants to tell them apart.

10:18.034 --> 10:20.745
But, Maomao, what about the embroidery?

10:20.828 --> 10:24.040
Weren’t the two working
on different pieces of embroidery?

10:24.123 --> 10:26.459
Yes, I’ve heard
they were embroidering animals.

10:26.542 --> 10:28.836
I think it was a bird and a rabbit.

10:29.378 --> 10:30.588
For example…

10:31.172 --> 10:33.299
what if the picture looked
something like this?

10:36.010 --> 10:38.054
If you flip this picture upside down,

10:38.137 --> 10:40.681
doesn’t the smiling face
look like an angry face?

10:42.266 --> 10:44.977
So, you’re saying the embroidery
was also an optical illusion?

10:46.187 --> 10:48.439
<i>If it were reflected in a mirror</i>
<i>and reversed left to right,</i>

10:49.148 --> 10:52.985
<i>the pattern might have looked like</i>
<i>something entirely different.</i>

10:53.069 --> 10:56.614
<i>While one of them was</i>
<i>embroidering by the southern window,</i>

10:56.697 --> 10:59.533
<i>the other could have slipped out</i>
<i>through the western entrance.</i>

10:59.617 --> 11:00.993
<i>I think that's possible.</i>

11:01.077 --> 11:02.578
I see…

11:02.662 --> 11:04.580
Certainly, with that method,

11:04.664 --> 11:07.667
it would be possible to sneak out
for a secret meeting.

11:07.750 --> 11:10.503
<i>The mirror brought by the foreign envoy…</i>

11:10.586 --> 11:12.838
<i>since it reflects so beautifully,</i>

11:12.922 --> 11:16.425
<i>it would be easy to mistake something</i>
<i>when seen from a distance.</i>

11:16.509 --> 11:20.012
<i>Long ago, my father studied abroad</i>
<i>in a western country</i>

11:20.096 --> 11:23.891
<i>and he said that embroidery was</i>
<i>a high-class privilege for children.</i>

11:24.517 --> 11:25.726
<i>Lord Gaoshun said</i>

11:25.810 --> 11:27.686
<i>that a young woman from a good family</i>

11:27.770 --> 11:29.647
<i>snuck out of the house</i>
<i>and became pregnant.</i>

11:30.398 --> 11:33.025
<i>I'm skeptical about</i>
<i>how much of that is true.</i>

11:33.651 --> 11:35.277
<i>What he is actually hiding…</i>

11:35.361 --> 11:37.655
<i>might be a completely different secret.</i>

11:38.906 --> 11:41.450
<i>There are times when someone</i>
<i>suspected of being a spy</i>

11:41.534 --> 11:43.160
<i>is welcomed as a guest.</i>

11:43.911 --> 11:47.623
<i>However, I don’t dig too deeply</i>
<i>into matters like that.</i>

11:47.706 --> 11:49.959
<i>Rather…</i>

11:52.294 --> 11:55.297
I’m more curious about what
I could make with this bear bile.

11:59.677 --> 12:03.722
The most beautiful woman
who sheds tears of pearl?

12:05.141 --> 12:07.893
The high-ranking officials in charge of
reception begged me to bring her.

12:08.477 --> 12:11.647
Lord Jinshi, you don’t have to go out
of your way to add extra work.

12:12.231 --> 12:13.983
I know!

12:16.152 --> 12:18.112
What were those envoys thinking,

12:18.195 --> 12:20.948
bringing those mirrors and all?

12:23.033 --> 12:25.661
Apothecary. Have you heard the story of

12:25.744 --> 12:28.080
a beautiful woman
shedding tears of pearls?

12:31.250 --> 12:32.084
What is it?

12:32.168 --> 12:34.295
<i>If it's a beautiful woman,</i>
<i>she’s right in front of you.</i>

12:34.378 --> 12:36.297
<i>I wish I could say that.</i>

12:38.174 --> 12:40.426
What does "tears of pearls" mean?

12:41.260 --> 12:43.012
I don’t know the details, but…

12:44.346 --> 12:47.016
<i>She was a beauty like the moon spirit,</i>

12:47.099 --> 12:48.017
<i>and when she danced,</i>

12:48.100 --> 12:50.603
<i>light would swirl as if to bless her,</i>

12:51.145 --> 12:54.440
<i>and her tears turned into pearls,</i>
<i>which then fell.</i>

12:55.483 --> 12:58.652
Apparently, she was a courtesan
from the pleasure district.

12:58.736 --> 13:02.114
A moon spirit?
Why the sudden mention of that?

13:02.198 --> 13:04.658
It’s the wish of the envoy
who is here now.

13:05.493 --> 13:07.578
Envoy, you mean from the West?

13:09.538 --> 13:11.665
<i>When the envoy was young,</i>

13:11.749 --> 13:14.502
<i>they often heard stories from</i>
<i>their grandfather about the moon spirit.</i>

13:15.669 --> 13:19.590
So, they asked me to find her
because they want to meet her.

13:19.673 --> 13:23.385
Their grandfather, huh?
That must have been a long time ago.

13:25.054 --> 13:26.388
It’s an impossible request, but

13:26.472 --> 13:28.349
they’re an important diplomatic figure.

13:28.432 --> 13:29.892
I want to do everything I can.

13:30.768 --> 13:32.978
Have you heard any rumors about it?

13:34.688 --> 13:35.940
<i>Fifty years ago…</i>

13:36.524 --> 13:37.942
<i>A dancer from the pleasure district…</i>

13:38.025 --> 13:39.735
<i>The moon spirit…</i>

13:40.903 --> 13:43.531
Of course,
this is a story from decades ago,

13:43.614 --> 13:45.783
so I don’t even know if she’s still alive.

13:45.866 --> 13:47.117
She’s alive.

13:47.743 --> 13:49.203
Is that true!

13:49.286 --> 13:50.621
True or not,

13:50.704 --> 13:53.999
you’ve met her, Lord Jinshi.
In the pleasure district.

13:54.583 --> 13:56.168
-Me?
-Yes.

13:56.252 --> 13:59.880
I don’t recall meeting anyone
who fits that description.

13:59.964 --> 14:02.967
It’s understandable
that you can't remember her right away.

14:04.051 --> 14:06.303
-Could it be…?
-That's right.

14:07.513 --> 14:10.307
<i>It’s the Granny. From the Rokushoukan.</i>

14:12.351 --> 14:14.395
Well, who is she?

14:16.772 --> 14:20.192
I believe she’ll come immediately
if money is offered.

14:20.276 --> 14:23.320
-What will you do?
-No, no, I don't think…

14:24.113 --> 14:26.949
But the other party knows
that she’s a person

14:27.032 --> 14:28.951
from 50 years ago, right?

14:29.034 --> 14:31.036
Isn’t a replacement beauty fine then?

14:31.120 --> 14:32.913
About that…

14:32.997 --> 14:35.958
I already arranged
a banquet with beauties.

14:36.876 --> 14:38.752
<i>They may not be as beautiful</i>
<i>as the moon spirit,</i>

14:38.836 --> 14:41.297
<i>but I gathered quite a selection.</i>

14:45.968 --> 14:48.470
<i>Yet the other party didn’t seem satisfied,</i>

14:48.554 --> 14:50.639
<i>and in fact, they laughed derisively.</i>

14:50.723 --> 14:53.017
<i>What kind of people are they?</i>

14:53.100 --> 14:55.352
Excuse me, but those beauties…

14:55.436 --> 14:58.188
-Did they accompany them at night--
-Maomao!

14:58.272 --> 15:00.608
That approach didn't work.

15:01.442 --> 15:03.110
<i>The envoy is a woman, after all.</i>

15:04.528 --> 15:07.615
<i>Oh, so that’s how the conversation</i>
<i>ended up with Lord Jinshi.</i>

15:08.324 --> 15:10.326
<i>He possesses a beauty</i>
<i>that would captivate anyone,</i>

15:10.409 --> 15:12.286
<i>and his gender is technically male.</i>

15:12.912 --> 15:15.205
<i>He is more than capable</i>
<i>of making women fall for him,</i>

15:15.289 --> 15:16.874
<i>a truly exceptional talent.</i>

15:16.957 --> 15:19.335
<i>However, trouble may also arise.</i>

15:20.377 --> 15:23.422
<i>If his charm is taken seriously</i>
<i>and they ask for a night together,</i>

15:23.505 --> 15:24.840
<i>there’s nothing he can do.</i>

15:25.466 --> 15:27.509
<i>Of course, despite being a woman</i>

15:27.593 --> 15:29.511
<i>with her position as envoy,</i>

15:29.595 --> 15:32.348
<i>she likely wouldn’t engage</i>
<i>in such a foolish act,</i>

15:32.431 --> 15:34.350
<i>but it's better to avoid it all together.</i>

15:35.517 --> 15:39.271
How important
is this "envoy," I wonder?

15:39.355 --> 15:42.566
She controls the trading posts
in the West and North.

15:42.650 --> 15:43.734
Does that give you an idea?

15:43.817 --> 15:46.779
The reason this caravan is so large,

15:46.862 --> 15:49.865
is that both sides want to
advance discussions on new trade.

15:50.574 --> 15:51.951
I see.

15:52.034 --> 15:55.079
I’ve heard that in distant countries,
inter-country marriages are common,

15:55.162 --> 15:58.165
and there are beautiful men
and women everywhere.

15:59.208 --> 16:02.670
<i>For someone from such a country</i>
<i>to call that Granny a "moon spirit."</i>

16:03.671 --> 16:06.590
Do you think they mixed some kind of
hallucinogen into the incense?

16:06.674 --> 16:08.550
Would they really do such a thing?

16:08.634 --> 16:10.761
I don't think so, but it's probably
the easiest way.

16:11.387 --> 16:13.889
If you did that,
it would become a diplomatic issue.

16:15.140 --> 16:16.934
At this point, anything will do.

16:17.017 --> 16:18.894
Do you have any information
from back then?

16:19.520 --> 16:21.480
<i>He must be really troubled.</i>

16:21.981 --> 16:24.400
<i>Well, if he's that desperate…</i>

16:26.485 --> 16:28.362
I’m sorry to have you
come all the way here.

16:31.448 --> 16:33.867
This is quite an odd story you’ve brought.

16:33.951 --> 16:36.787
This place is pretty grim, huh?

16:36.870 --> 16:38.914
Don’t you offer a cup of tea or something?

16:39.415 --> 16:41.875
Well, this is a meeting room.

16:42.835 --> 16:44.336
Old woman,

16:44.420 --> 16:47.089
you hosted an envoy from
a foreign country long ago, didn’t you?

16:47.172 --> 16:49.174
Ah, yes, I did.

16:49.258 --> 16:51.552
It was over 50 years ago, I think.

16:51.635 --> 16:53.971
It was during the reign
of the previous, previous ruler.

16:54.930 --> 16:57.975
<i>Originally, there was a town</i>
<i>built using ruins,</i>

16:58.058 --> 17:00.978
<i>and many people came for sightseeing.</i>

17:01.061 --> 17:03.647
<i>Because it was a place</i>
<i>with a lot of people coming and going,</i>

17:03.731 --> 17:05.566
<i>there was apparently a bit of a conflict</i>

17:05.649 --> 17:08.152
<i>when it was suddenly decided</i>
<i>to make it the capital.</i>

17:08.777 --> 17:11.447
<i>The capital had just moved</i>
<i>and there was no great castle,</i>

17:11.530 --> 17:13.991
<i>so there was no place to host visitors.</i>

17:14.074 --> 17:16.326
<i>The ruler was quite troubled,</i>

17:16.410 --> 17:19.872
<i>and in the end, it was decided to use</i>
<i>the remaining ruins to host them.</i>

17:19.955 --> 17:21.665
<i>It used to be</i>
<i>some kind of ceremonial hall.</i>

17:21.749 --> 17:25.502
<i>And near the fruit orchard,</i>
<i>there was a beautiful pond and buildings.</i>

17:26.086 --> 17:27.254
<i>Is that…?</i>

17:28.088 --> 17:30.466
<i>On the north side of the rear palace</i>
<i>which I visited recently,</i>

17:30.549 --> 17:32.426
<i>there was a ruined fruit orchard.</i>

17:32.509 --> 17:34.553
<i>It wouldn't be surprising if the venue</i>

17:34.636 --> 17:37.431
<i>for the banquet at that time</i>
<i>was now inside the rear palace.</i>

17:37.514 --> 17:40.726
As the lead dancer on that stage,

17:40.809 --> 17:43.604
I was chosen from the pleasure district.

17:44.271 --> 17:45.522
Why were you chosen?

17:45.606 --> 17:47.357
Well, that's because…

17:47.441 --> 17:49.985
I was the highest-ranked courtesan
at the time.

17:50.069 --> 17:52.613
I danced with a dozen
or so others as the main star.

17:53.489 --> 17:55.491
<i>Now, you look more like a withered branch</i>

17:55.574 --> 17:57.242
<i>than a flower.</i>

17:57.326 --> 18:00.579
But well, the main reason
was probably my physique.

18:00.662 --> 18:01.622
Huh?

18:02.331 --> 18:04.083
<i>I was tall…</i>

18:04.166 --> 18:06.126
<i>and had a well-defined body.</i>

18:06.794 --> 18:09.421
<i>Certainly, if you're going to stand</i>
<i>on stage as the lead,</i>

18:09.505 --> 18:11.632
<i>a larger body would be better.</i>

18:11.715 --> 18:12.966
But you know,

18:13.050 --> 18:14.802
since it was an improvised setting,

18:14.885 --> 18:16.929
I struggled with the preparations.

18:17.679 --> 18:20.140
<i>I even calculated the phases of the moon,</i>

18:20.224 --> 18:22.601
<i>and to improve the view from the banquet,</i>

18:22.684 --> 18:24.436
<i>I removed any obstacles.</i>

18:25.437 --> 18:28.190
<i>Since the orchard was nearby,</i>
<i>there were lots of insects,</i>

18:28.273 --> 18:30.150
<i>so I had to remove</i>
<i>every single caterpillar</i>

18:30.234 --> 18:32.820
<i>from the leaves beforehand.</i>

18:32.903 --> 18:33.904
<i>In the end,</i>

18:33.987 --> 18:36.990
<i>the insects still gathered around</i>
<i>due to the torches.</i>

18:37.533 --> 18:39.660
<i>Even though I prepared all that,</i>

18:39.743 --> 18:43.288
<i>on the day of the event, there were people</i>
<i>who played pranks on my outfit.</i>

18:44.081 --> 18:46.667
<i>They rubbed insect corpses onto it.</i>

18:47.584 --> 18:50.170
<i>But I was not weak.</i>

18:50.254 --> 18:53.090
<i>I hid it with fabric</i>
<i>and managed to pull it off.</i>

18:53.173 --> 18:55.175
<i>The result was a great success!</i>

18:55.259 --> 18:57.678
<i>The person who played the prank</i>
<i>was regretful.</i>

18:57.761 --> 19:01.431
<i>I've heard that story many times.</i>
<i>Isn't there something else?</i>

19:01.515 --> 19:04.017
You're not a cute one, huh!

19:04.101 --> 19:04.977
Ouch…

19:11.275 --> 19:14.695
<i>It's a beautiful painting.</i>
<i>It's the first time I've seen it.</i>

19:14.778 --> 19:16.989
<i>The old woman must have cherished it.</i>

19:18.448 --> 19:21.160
<i>For this fantastical beauty</i>

19:21.243 --> 19:23.537
<i>to become a slave to gold.</i>

19:25.372 --> 19:27.833
It seems that the envoy

19:27.916 --> 19:31.420
went all the way back to his home country
to have it painted by a painter.

19:31.503 --> 19:33.505
He named this painting "Moon Goddess."

19:33.589 --> 19:37.301
I see. So this painting
has been beautified as well.

19:37.384 --> 19:38.969
Did you say something?

19:39.052 --> 19:40.762
Nothing.

19:41.346 --> 19:44.808
That envoy never set foot
on this land again,

19:45.684 --> 19:48.604
but he entrusted
the caravan to deliver it.

19:49.730 --> 19:51.523
But, old woman,

19:51.607 --> 19:53.609
you just did your usual work, right?

19:53.692 --> 19:55.277
Why were you so well-liked?

19:55.360 --> 19:58.530
I don't know that either.

20:01.283 --> 20:05.037
<i>The old woman is someone</i>
<i>who can view things objectively.</i>

20:05.120 --> 20:06.538
<i>There’s no exaggeration in her words.</i>

20:07.164 --> 20:08.123
<i>However…</i>

20:08.207 --> 20:11.460
<i>No matter how beautiful</i>
<i>the old woman was back then,</i>

20:12.628 --> 20:16.465
<i>why did they call her a Goddess?</i>

20:19.468 --> 20:21.053
I don’t understand.

20:21.136 --> 20:24.848
Well then, shall we search for someone
who resembles the woman in this painting?

20:24.932 --> 20:27.184
That’s all I can think of…

20:27.809 --> 20:31.313
<i>Honestly, it’ll be hard</i>
<i>to find a tall beauty</i>

20:31.396 --> 20:32.814
<i>who resembles this painting.</i>

20:33.315 --> 20:34.942
Why don’t we try finding a tall woman,

20:35.025 --> 20:37.527
even if her face doesn’t resemble hers?

20:38.278 --> 20:40.530
Although she’s quite shrunk now,

20:40.614 --> 20:43.784
back then she was said to be 175 cm tall.

20:43.867 --> 20:45.452
She was quite tall.

20:46.036 --> 20:48.413
Yes. Since she was good at dancing,

20:48.497 --> 20:51.416
having long arms and legs
made her look even more impressive.

20:51.500 --> 20:52.709
However,

20:52.793 --> 20:55.837
when it comes to finding
a tall beauty to match her,

20:55.921 --> 20:57.256
that is quite a challenge.

20:57.339 --> 21:00.300
The envoys are about that height as well,

21:00.384 --> 21:03.804
so if the beauty is too small,
she might look like a child.

21:04.721 --> 21:06.932
Envoys?

21:07.015 --> 21:08.600
It's not just one?

21:09.309 --> 21:12.312
Yes, they’re said to be cousins
who share the same grandfather.

21:13.480 --> 21:15.107
<i>The way he phrased that earlier,</i>

21:15.190 --> 21:17.818
<i>the envoys must</i>
<i>also be quite beautiful too.</i>

21:18.402 --> 21:19.569
<i>If that’s the case,</i>

21:19.653 --> 21:22.281
<i>they must find someone</i>
<i>who is over 175 cm tall</i>

21:22.364 --> 21:26.326
<i>with beauty so striking</i>
<i>that they could silence the envoys.</i>

21:29.496 --> 21:32.332
I found a very fitting person.

21:32.833 --> 21:36.420
A beauty who is over 175 cm tall, right?

21:43.176 --> 21:44.720
What are you trying to say?

23:46.007 --> 23:48.760
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:57.602 --> 24:00.397
<i>The next episode is "Moon Spirit."</i>

24:00.939 --> 24:01.815
Subtitle translation by:
Abhishek Chand Ramola
